@page
@model AboutModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "About Love Rallying";
}

<h1>@ViewData["Title"]</h1>

<p>Love Rallying is a project for rally fans, competitors, and event organisers. It brings rally events, entry lists, results, and competitor information together in one place, with a long-term goal of helping organisers run rallies through the platform.</p>

<h2>Rallying should be accessible to everyone</h2>
<p>More and more services are asking people to subscribe. I started Love Rallying because I wanted rally information to be easier to access without another recurring payment or a stream of adverts.</p>
<p><strong>Love Rallying is free to use, with no adverts.</strong> That’s a commitment. I want the service to remain useful and accessible to the rally community without putting core information behind a paywall.</p>

<h2>What you can explore</h2>
<p>Love Rallying is growing as more event information is added. You can currently browse events, including seeded and unseeded entry lists; explore car profiles and driver and co-driver profiles with results; and see Rescue and Recovery Units alongside the events they have attended.</p>
<p>The longer-term aim is to support event organisers in running rallies through the platform. If results can be published live, broadcasters could also use the API to show leaderboards during coverage. Competitors could build a record of their results, while fans could explore events and statistics.</p>

<h2>A home for rally photography</h2>
<p>I’d also like to make it easier to find event photographs. For example, you could look for photos of car 99 from the 2026 Plains Rally and follow a link to the photographer’s gallery to view or purchase them.</p>
<p>The photos would stay hosted by the photographer or their chosen platform. Love Rallying would help people find the right images without needing to store large photo collections itself.</p>

<h2>Built to keep costs low</h2>
<p>Keeping Love Rallying free means keeping its running costs manageable. The API and frontend run on Azure Web Apps, while Azure Table Storage holds the data.</p>
<p>I’m taking inspiration from Troy Hunt and Have I Been Pwned: a useful service can be built with a practical, cost-conscious architecture. I also plan to use Cloudflare for caching and protection. Caching can reduce unnecessary requests to the app and help keep the Azure resources needed to run the service small. Cloudflare is not in place yet.</p>

<h2>Built in the open</h2>
<p>The API and frontend are available on GitHub. I welcome people who want to help improve Love Rallying through development, issues, and feature ideas.</p>
